# Local development settings. Copy to `.env` and edit; `.env` is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Resolution order is ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE, then `.env`, then the default
# (engine/config.py). So exporting a value always beats this file, and this file
# always beats the built-in default.
#
# THIS FILE IS FOR DEVELOPMENT MACHINES. On the server, settings belong in the
# systemd unit -- `.env` is not deployed, is not tracked, and a stale one is
# exactly the sort of invisible state DEPLOY.md's "never edit a tracked file on
# the server" rule exists to prevent.

# --- the store -------------------------------------------------------------
# libpq URLs (docs/POSTGRES_PLAN.md). The defaults are libpq's own -- database
# `bvp` over the local socket as the OS user, which is what the server has.
# A development machine names its own cluster here. The TEST url is a
# maintenance database on a server the test suite may CREATE and DROP
# databases on; it is never the store itself.

# BVP_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://bvp@127.0.0.1:54329/bvp
# BVP_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://bvp@127.0.0.1:54329/postgres

# --- paths -----------------------------------------------------------------
# All optional; each defaults to the matching directory in the repo root.

# BVP_DATA_DIR=data
# BVP_REFERENCE_DIR=reference

# --- the second fixture calendar -------------------------------------------
# `1` enables the `calendar` step in services/run_cycle.py, which pulls a 7-day
# fixture window from BBC scores-fixtures pages. Anything else leaves it off.
#
# READ docs/OUTSTANDING.md 4.5 BEFORE SETTING THIS TO 1. It is a pre-release
# validation aid with a recorded exit condition -- retire it when a commercial
# fixture feed is sourced, or at public launch, whichever comes first. It must
# not be running when the product is commercial.

BVP_BBC_CALENDAR=0

# Full-time results from the same pages (services/bbc_results): settles tips
# before football-data publishes the season's file. Same decision, same exit
# condition as the calendar; a separate switch so either can run alone.
BVP_BBC_RESULTS=0

# --- the betPawa scrape ----------------------------------------------------
# `1` enables the `betpawa` step in services/run_cycle.py: one request a
# morning to www.betpawa.ug for the event and selection ids behind the site's
# "bet this on betPawa" buttons (docs/BETPAWA_PLAN.md). Additive, never fatal.
BVP_BETPAWA=0

# --- geocoding -------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed to rebuild reference/stadiums.csv (services/stadium_coords).
# Read by that tool directly, not through engine/config.py.

# LOCATIONIQ_API_KEY=

# --- sign-in ---------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/AUTH_PLAN.md. The Google OAuth client id is public (it is the `aud` of
# every ID token) but it is environment, not code; the server carries it in
# the bvp-api unit. Sign-in answers 401 while it is empty.

# BVP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com

# Development is http://localhost, and a Secure cookie is never sent there.
# The server keeps the default (1).
BVP_COOKIE_SECURE=0

# Sliding session length in days.
# BVP_SESSION_DAYS=30
